    note for GameController "Opening exam core and JavaFX presentation are implemented.<br/>Midterm Continue/Retake explicitly report T10.<br/>Combat backend exists with explicit policy.<br/>Opening cues and dialogue exist, Final policy remains pending."
    note for GameState "HP is separate from marks and energy.<br/>Returned snapshots are defensive copies.<br/>Relationships/rewards are persisted data, not playable systems yet."
    note for RuleValues "Null is TBD, never zero.<br/>No production balancing defaults.<br/>Separate opt-in Demo supplies provisional values."
    note for ContentCatalog "One settlement: participate then response, OR quiet.<br/>ClassroomScreen and LessonMenu already wire both menu levels.<br/>Day 1 raises hand; Day 2 asks a chosen question.<br/>Fixed ordinary questions, supplied major sample size.<br/>Demo supplies four lessons and two Hub activities.<br/>Assessment banks and later content remain pending."
    note for GradeBook "65 Term / 10 Participation / 25 Final.<br/>Midterm belongs to Term; its weight is supplied explicitly.<br/>First two absences free, then minus one overall percentage point."
    note for AssessmentRecord "Ordinary including makeup: three-day delay.<br/>Midterm and Final: immediate result, no skip.<br/>Evaluator supplies mark; no HP or automatic rubric conversion."
    note for SaveManager "Only active DAY_END snapshots.<br/>Load does not advance or regrant effects.<br/>Ending/Retake autosave boundaries remain T12."
    note for JavaAssessmentRunner "Actual compiler and test processes with time/output limits.<br/>Trusted local code only, not an OS security sandbox.<br/>No automatic course-score rubric."

    note for Main "Opens the JavaFX game window only.<br/>Arguments are ignored: no CLI routes, modes or day jumps.<br/>FXGL and libGDX are prepared by Gradle, not started."
    note for GameSession "Frontend adapter: never edits GameState directly.<br/>Rejected/Pending actions retain state.<br/>A late opening action can succeed by settling TIMEOUT only.<br/>showLesson() is called once per class."
    note for OpeningScreen "UI stages are presentation, not a second combat state machine.<br/>Polls the core throughout turns, log and animations.<br/>No independent deadline or HP/grade calculations.<br/>Timeout closes the current presentation path, ending plays once."
    note for OpeningEndingScreen "Reads the finished OpeningBattle.Ending.<br/>Grade stamp and story, no battle stats.<br/>After dialogue: BEGIN SUMMER SCHOOL calls completeOpening once.<br/>Success routes through AppContext to DayIntroScreen and fresh Day 1.<br/>This is the opening result page, not the pending semester-ending system."
    note for FastForward "Shared keyboard/mouse hold state for dialogue and transitions.<br/>Never changes the backend exam clock or selects an answer."
    note for Hud "HP/SAN visual feedback follows backend snapshots.<br/>SanBar and XpBreakdown are display-only, not new stat policies."
    note for CombatEvaluations "One evaluation at a time; results return on the UI thread.<br/>Leaving the combat drops late results.<br/>A failed or refused result keeps the ticket and work for a retry."
    note for CombatScreen "Displays the backend view only: no UI timing, weights, HP or marks.<br/>No pause while a question's clock runs.<br/>No evaluator shipped: submission reports T06 (Lab) or T07."
    note for SlideProjector "A lecture line starting with a slide:name cue turns to that slide.<br/>Presentation only: never calls the core.<br/>Large view pauses the lecture until closed."
    note for LessonMenu "Opening or leaving a menu calls nothing in the core.<br/>Only the final response or quiet settles, once, for the captured lesson day."
    note for DialogueHistory "Window state only, never saved.<br/>Holding the advance key fast-forwards; a held key never makes a choice."
    note for AudioDirector "Same cue keeps playing across screens; a new cue cross-fades.<br/>Missing or unplayable files are silent and listed.<br/>Sound never changes game state."
    note for LabRunService "One run at a time; results return on the UI thread.<br/>Edits make older results stale.<br/>Evidence-to-mark is T06; Lab problems not supplied yet."

    GameController --> CombatRules : explicit decisions
    GameState *-- CombatSession : copied transient assessment state
    CombatSession --> Question : difficulty-ranked content
    note for CombatRules "30s soft threshold and Combo +5 are confirmed.<br/>HP formula, score conversion and ambiguous composition require explicit policy."
    note for CombatSession "Backend monotonic clock and stale-result tickets.<br/>Final completed answer gets Dasher.<br/>Reward delays are not inventory/effect operations.<br/>No mid-combat save."

    class OpeningContent {
        +load(String resource) OpeningContent$
        +questions() List~QuestionView~
        +initialStudent() StudentState
        +intro() List~String~
        +defeat() List~String~
        +victory() List~String~
    }
    class OpeningBattle {
        +totalTimeLimit() Duration$
        +timeLimit(int ordinal) Duration$
        -long battleStarted
        -long lastObserved
        -long finishedElapsedNanos
        ~copy() OpeningBattle
        ~view(long now) OpeningView
        ~tick(long now) void
    }
    %% Diagram aliases: OpeningView = OpeningBattle.View, OpeningEnding = OpeningBattle.Ending.
    class OpeningView {
        <<nested record>>
        +Phase phase
        +StudentState student
        +int ducksRemaining
        +boolean usingDuck
        +Duration remaining
        +clockRunning() boolean
        +List~Feedback~ answers
        +OpeningEnding ending
    }
    class OpeningEnding {
        <<nested record>>
        +int grade
        +DefeatReason reason
        +AnimationCue animation
        +List~String~ dialogue
    }
    ContentCatalog o-- OpeningContent : optional explicit scenario
    GameState *-- OpeningBattle : ephemeral previous semester
    GameController --> OpeningBattle : copy and settle
    OpeningBattle --> OpeningContent : authored keys and story
    OpeningBattle ..> OpeningView : immutable observation
    OpeningView --> OpeningEnding
    note for OpeningBattle "Initial HP 9, no upper cap, one duck.<br/>One HP per impact, immediate zero-HP pass-out.<br/>Battle start anchors one continuous 180-second clock.<br/>Turns and all animations consume time until an ending.<br/>Reveal completion permits answers, no clock reset.<br/>Expired actions settle TIMEOUT first, no late HP loss.<br/>Answers cost no HP, clockRunning means unfinished.<br/>Both endings enter unchanged Day 1."
    note for OpeningEnding "67 defeat or pass-out, 89 victory.<br/>Cues and dialogue drive frontend ending presentation.<br/>Never inserted into this term's GradeBook."
